You are checking whether newly proposed story records already exist. A scene was just absorbed, and the extraction proposed opening some NEW plot threads or commitments. A plot thread is an open narrative question; a commitment is an obligation someone owes (a promise, a threat or a piece of foreshadowing). Each proposed record is listed below as a row: its title, the beat the scene gave it, the transcript evidence the extraction cited, why the extraction called it new, and up to three existing records of the same type that look similar, each with its id, status, latest beats and the similarity signals that put it on the list.

Give exactly one decision per row:
